# LF on every OS: a Windows checkout defaults to CRLF, but the migrations are compiled in with include_str! and refinery
# checksums them (set_abort_divergent), so a CRLF build would refuse a database migrated by an LF build, and the
# reverse. The tests also compare SQL text with migration/04.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Built and vendored files: byte-for-byte, so the CSS check in CI compares like with like on Windows.
server/assets/** -text
styles/vendor/** -text
*.sh text eol=lf
